{{!-- partials/option-label
     A select/radio option's text: its label, plus a marker when the field no
     longer declares the value.

     A stored value outside `options` is kept as a selected option so re-saving
     the form doesn't drop it — the marker is what tells the editor that the
     value is on its way out and that picking another one is one-way. `<option>`
     text carries no markup, so the marker is plain text; the `data-unlisted`
     attribute on the element carries the same fact for styling.

     Context: one entry of a field's `options` (used inside `{{#each options}}`). --}}
{{label}}
{{#if unlisted}}
  {{t "option_no_longer_offered"}}
{{/if}}
